.Li 0 ,
.Li false ,
.Li f
turn it off), the flag overrides it (the env default for systemd
EnvironmentFile installs).
.It Ev SSH3_PASSWORD_SYSTEM
The ParseBool default of
.Fl -password-system
.Pf ( Li 1 ,
.Li true ,
.Li t
wire the verifier,
.Li 0 ,
.Li false ,
.Li f
close it), the explicit
.Fl -password-system Cm on | off
overrides it (the env default for systemd EnvironmentFile installs).
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_UNAUTH_CONVERSATIONS
The env default of
.Fl -max-unauth-conversations ,
the flag overrides it; an unparsable or negative value falls back
to the default.
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_PASSWORD_FAILURES
The env default of
.Fl -max-password-failures ,
the flag overrides it; an unparsable or non-positive value falls
back to the default.
.It Ev SSH3_PASSWORD_LOCKOUT_SECONDS
The env default of
.Fl -password-lockout-seconds ,
the flag overrides it; an unparsable or negative value falls back
to the default.
.It Ev SSH3_PERMIT_OPEN
The default of
.Fl -permit-open
(and of the
.Fl o Cm PermitOpen
option);
the flag overrides it, an unset or empty value keeps the
unrestricted dial.
.It Ev SSH3_PERMIT_LISTEN
The default of
.Fl -permit-listen
(and of the
.Fl o Cm PermitListen
option); the flag overrides it.
.It Ev SSH3_GATEWAY_PORTS
The default of
.Fl -gateway-ports
(and of the
.Fl o Cm GatewayPorts
option),
.Cm no | yes | clientspecified ;
the flag overrides it, an unknown value keeps the default.
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_SFTP_SESSIONS_PER_USER
The env default of
.Fl -max-sftp-sessions-per-user ,
the flag overrides it.
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_CONNECTIONS
The env default of
.Fl -max-connections ,
the flag overrides it.
.It Ev SSH3_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS
The env default of
.Fl -handshake-timeout-ms ,
the flag overrides it.
.It Ev SSH3_MAX_REVERSE_FORWARDS
The env default of
.Fl -max-reverse-forwards ,
the flag overrides it.
.It Ev SSH3_SFTP_JAIL
The SFTP isolation mode,
.Cm chroot
or
.Cm lexical ,
same as
.Fl -sftp-jail ;
the flag overrides it, an unknown value keeps the default.
.It Ev SSH3C_PROTO
With
.Li 1 ,
machine-readable INTEROP-* markers go to stdout (the interop runner
protocol); production runs log one-liners instead.
.It Ev S3_OIDC_CA_FILE
Pins the HTTPS trust store of the OIDC discovery/JWKS fetches.
.It Ev SHELL
The program the session channels execute (default
.Pa /bin/sh ) .
.It Ev LISTEN_PID , Ev LISTEN_FDS
Read-only protocol of
.Xr sd_listen_fds 3 :
present together, the passed UDP sockets serve and
.Fl l
is not required; the markers are unset before any child is forked.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/ssh3/authorized_keys"
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/authorized_identities
First file of the default identities chain (the reference
DefaultIdentitiesFileNames), read for the session user when no
.Fl K
is given; missing files are tolerated.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
Second file of the default identities chain, the sshd shape.
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/cert.pem
TLS certificate (packaged default of
.Fl c ,
read by the service).
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/key.pem
TLS private key (packaged default of
.Fl k ,
mode 0640, owner-readable by the service only).
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/authorized_keys
Authorized keys (typical
.Fl K
target).
.El
.Sh SOCKET ACTIVATION
The packaged
.Pa ssh3-server.socket
binds UDP/443 as root and systemd passes the ready datagram socket to
the service:
.Nm
takes the fds at fd 3 upward, one or two serve.  A bare
.Li ListenDatagram=443
hands over ONE dual-stack IPv6 socket
.Pq BindIPv6Only=default ;
a
.Li 0.0.0.0:443
plus
.Li [::]:443
pair hands over TWO, each becomes its own listener and a connection
stays on the fd it arrived on.  Each fd is verified to be a datagram
socket of either family, set nonblocking and close-on-exec, the
LISTEN_* markers are unset and
.Xr bind 2
is never called; the IPv6 mode of the unit
.Pq IPV6_V6ONLY
is served as handed over and logged.
No capability
.Pq CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
is needed by the service; under the default privilege model the
service is root with a minimal bounding set (the per-session setuid
capabilities only), see
.Sx PRIVILEGE MODEL
and
.Pa ssh3-server.service .
An fd of the wrong type or family, or more than two, stops the daemon
with an error instead of falling back to a second bind.
The listener address and port are owned by the socket unit
.Xr systemd.socket 5 .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGTERM Ns / Ns Dv SIGINT
Graceful shutdown: new connections are answered with
CONNECTION_CLOSE, the active conversations drain up to
.Ev SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN
seconds, then the leftovers close, the session children are killed
and the daemon exits 0.  A repeated signal closes everything at once.
.It Dv SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.El
